  "mechanisms": {
    "composition": "Production Ninja compiles mngrayc.c twice with different private precomp search roots and local selectors. DrawState context selects ClientDrawState/DrawStateA/W/BltColor; button-blit selects only BitBltSysBmp renamed wow_button_BitBltSysBmp. Inspect both; do not report one as unused based on the other.",
    "original": "ClientDrawState retains validation, mono/default/disabled/union effects, callback dispatch, text/icon/bitmap drawing and BltColor. PSMTextOut/PSMGetTextExtent and MBToWCSEx resolve other C objects; native GDI/critical-section calls resolve Windows. Four stable IDs for icon size/PolyPatBlt/brushes are already eliminated through B providers.",
    "drawScope": "F wow_control_draw_state creates caller-scoped scratch DC/bitmap/atlas, saves TLS, invokes original ClientDrawState and restores/releases in finally. Its SelectObject adapter tracks newly selected scratch bitmaps for cleanup; arbitrary callback selections do not transfer ownership. Current code has original-body selection failure and finally patches; not modified or newly approved by this ownership audit.",
    "buttonScope": "F wow_button_current_resources obtains current Button invocation, lazily initializes atlas and copies current display depth. Scope leave releases resources and any deferred lookaside value. Button and enclosing DrawState may nest; they cannot share a mutable current-resource pointer without explicit nesting ownership. This demonstrates current distinct lifetimes, not permanent approval of two public binding families.",
    "resourceAbi": "wow_button_resources includes original OEMBITMAPINFO/OBI_COUNT through opennt_user_multipass. A header-only relocation to B would retain B->C coupling. S14 must decide original type/declaration placement; S13 separates invocation owner from reusable native resource operations without a second registry.",
    "method": "Complete source and both precomp files read, actual production defines/COFF/VALID deps/maps inspected, current drawing and Button scope owners traced. No new runtime execution."
  },
